(b)
$\begin{align*}z_X&=\frac{48-40}{4}\\&=2\end{align*}$
For $y=270$, $z_Y=1.5$. The score $48$ on the $X$ scale is more extreme: it lies $2$ standard deviations above the mean, compared with $1.5$.
